course: dictionary
lesson: 15905
title: Unmeasured
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Unmeasured is a word you can take apart. The un- at the start means not, and measured means had its size, amount or value found. So unmeasured means not measured: nobody has found out how big, how much or how great something is. «The bag of sand was unmeasured, so nobody knew how heavy it was.» The clue is the words "nobody knew how heavy", which tell you no weight was ever found.
explain: In maths and science, unmeasured usually means that a length, angle or amount still needs a ruler, protractor or scale. «The scientists left the depth of the pond unmeasured, so their results were weak.» If an important thing is not measured, the results cannot be trusted as much. Always ask: what is missing here? The answer is often the measurement.
explain: Writers also use unmeasured in a literary way, to mean without limit, too great to measure. «She gave her family an unmeasured love that filled the whole house.» Here nobody could measure her love, because it had no end. Try your meaning in the sentence: "a love with no limit" still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: Unmeasured means not measured; nobody has found its size, amount or value.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so you can work out unmeasured from measured.
fact: «The bag of sand was unmeasured, so nobody knew how heavy it was.»
fact: In poetry or stories, «unmeasured love» means love that is too great to measure, with no limit.
fact: In science, unmeasured results are weak evidence, because important things were not measured.
exercise: «The recipe said to add an unmeasured amount of flour.» What does unmeasured mean here? | Measured very carefully | Exactly one cup | Lost forever | *Not measured, so nobody knows the exact amount
exercise: Which word means not measured? | measured | protractor | *unmeasured | ruler
exercise: A science report says, «The temperature was left unmeasured.» Why is this a problem? | Because temperature is always the same | Because the report is in the wrong colour | Because the report is too long to read | *Because an important thing was not measured, so the results are weak
test: «Her unmeasured love for her family filled the whole house.» What does unmeasured suggest here? | Small and hard to see | Measured by a ruler | Sad and lonely | *So great it has no limit, too big to measure
test: A maths sheet has an unmeasured angle. Which tool do you need to measure it? | A recipe book | A whisper | *A protractor | A ruler
exam: Ben says unmeasured means not measured yet. Is he right? | No, it means very small | *Yes, nobody has found its size, amount or value | No, it means too hot to touch | No, it means painted
